    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1801.07238v1</id>
    <title>On a Helly-type question for central symmetry</title>
    <updated>2018-01-22T18:40:59Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.07238v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1801.07238v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We study a certain Helly-type question by Konrad Swanepoel. Assume that $X$ is a set of points such that every $k$-subset of $X$ is in centrally symmetric convex position, is it true that $X$ must also be in centrally symmetric convex position? It is easy to see that this is false if $k\le 5$, but it may be true for sufficiently large $k$. We investigate this question and give some partial results.</summary>
